title: 'pallet-psm-remote-tests: support multi-instance fungibles and Location selector'

doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `pallet-psm-remote-tests`: snapshot now fetches storage from a configurable
    list of pallet names (`assets_pallet_names: Vec<String>`), enabling tests
    against runtimes whose `Fungibles` is a union over multiple `pallet_assets`
    instances.

    `remote-ext-tests-psm` CLI: `--asset-id <u32>` is replaced with
    `--asset-location <JSON>` accepting any `xcm::v5::Location`. Default
    behaviour is unchanged (USDT, trust-backed asset `1984`).

    The Asset Hub Westend wiring fetches both `Assets` and `ForeignAssets`
    storage, so foreign-registered external stablecoins can be exercised
    directly.

    Breaking changes:
    - `PsmTestConfig::assets_pallet_name: String` -> `assets_pallet_names: Vec<String>`
    - `build_ext`'s second parameter changes from `String` to `Vec<String>`

crates:
- name: pallet-psm-remote-tests
  bump: major
- name: remote-ext-tests-psm
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-psm
  bump: none
